---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro'

const appUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_URL ?? 'http://localhost:5173'
const contactEmail = 'legal@tarione.com'
const effectiveDate = '16 April 2026'
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Tari1"
  description="The terms and conditions governing your use of the Tari1 platform."
>
  <Navbar activePage="terms" />

  <main class="hero-gradient pt-20 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-[#ffddb8] text-[#121c28] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-6">
        Legal
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-primary tracking-tight mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-12">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base">
        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">1. Agreement to terms</h2>
          <p>
            By creating an account or using the Tari1 platform ("Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you are using Tari1 on behalf of an organisation, you represent that you have authority to bind that organisation to these Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">2. Description of service</h2>
          <p>
            Tari1 is a cloud-based invoicing and financial management platform that allows businesses and freelancers to create invoices, accept payments, track expenses, generate financial reports, and prepare tax filing packs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">3. Accounts</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>You must provide accurate and complete information when registering.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for maintaining password security and account activities.</li>
            <li>Notify us immediately at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">{contactEmail}</a> of any unauthorized access.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">4. Subscription plans, billing, and cancellation</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Paid plans are billed on a monthly or annual basis via <strong>Paystack</strong>.</li>
            <li>Prices are in NGN and are inclusive of VAT unless otherwise stated.</li>
            <li>Subscriptions auto-renew unless cancelled. You may cancel at any time through <strong>Settings &gt; Billing</strong> in your dashboard.</li>
            <li>Cancellations take effect at the end of your current billing period. You retain access until then.</li>
            <li><strong>Free trial:</strong> New accounts receive a 30-day free trial with no credit card required. If you do not upgrade before day 30, your account will be temporarily locked. You may unlock it at any time by selecting a paid plan — no data is deleted.</li>
            <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> All payments are final and non-refundable except where required by Nigerian consumer protection law. If you believe you have been billed in error, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">{contactEmail}</a> within 14 days of the charge.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">5. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to use Tari1 to violate laws, create fraudulent invoices, transmit malware, or scrape the platform.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">6. Tax and compliance</h2>
          <p>
            Tari1 provides helpful data compilation tools. This does not constitute tax, accounting, or compliance advice. Consult a tax professional before filing. We are not liable for tax penalties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">7. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">
            To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Tari1's total liability to you for any claim arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Service shall not exceed the greater of (a) the total fees paid by you in the three months immediately preceding the claim, or (b) ₦10,000.
          </p>
          <p>
            In no event shall Tari1 be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special, or punitive damages, including loss of profits, data, or goodwill, even if advised of the possibility of such damages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-card p-8 rounded-[24px] shadow-sm border border-outline-variant">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-primary mb-3">8. Governing law and disputes</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the <strong>Federal Republic of Nigeria</strong>. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Lagos State, Nigeria. You agree to attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute informally by contacting us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">{contactEmail}</a> before initiating legal proceedings.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="w-full py-12 bg-surface border-t border-outline-variant">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-element-gap px-container-padding max-w-7xl mx-auto">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 items-center md:items-start">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary">Tari1</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary text-center md:text-left max-w-xs">
          © {new Date().getFullYear()} Tari1. All rights reserved. Built for the modern freelancer.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary text-center md:text-left">Lagos, Nigeria · <a href="mailto:legal@tarione.com" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">legal@tarione.com</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-8">
        <a class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-primary transition-all" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-primary transition-all" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        <a class="text-sm text-text-secondary hover:text-primary transition-all" href="mailto:abubakar.sambo@tarione.com">Contact Support</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
